From: AerynOS packaging
Subject: [PATCH] libapparmor: avoid a variable length array inside a union

kernel.c sizes the scratch buffer in self_syscall_enabled_init_once()
from the total_size variable. Because total_size is a variable rather
than a constant expression, the array member is a variable length array
inside a union, which is a GCC extension that clang rejects outright:

  kernel.c:375:8: error: fields must have a constant size:
  'variable length array in structure' extension will never be supported

The value is sizeof(struct lsm_ctx) + 8, which is a constant expression
already, so spell it out in the declaration. total_size keeps its
initialiser and every later use of it is unchanged, so the buffer has
exactly the same size and layout as before.

--- a/libraries/libapparmor/src/kernel.c
+++ b/libraries/libapparmor/src/kernel.c
@@ -372,7 +372,7 @@ static void self_syscall_enabled_init_once(void)
 	__u32 total_size = sizeof(struct lsm_ctx) + 8;
 	union {
 		struct lsm_ctx ctx_buff;
-		char buff[total_size]; /* force allocate trailing space */
+		char buff[sizeof(struct lsm_ctx) + 8]; /* force allocate trailing space */
 	} buff;
 	struct lsm_ctx *ctx = &buff.ctx_buff;
 	
